    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="14">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 14</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LVIII. Se ðe hloþe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_14.lnote.oe.18"/> betygen sie, geswicne se hine be CXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_14.lnote.oe.19"/> hida oððe swa bete.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_14.lnote.oe.20"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe hloðe be::gen sie, geswicne he hine be CXX hida oððe swa bete.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe hloðe betogen sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_14.lnote.oe.5"/>, geswicne se hine be CXX hida oððe bete swa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe hloðe betogen sy, geclensie se hine be hundtwelftigu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> hida oððe swa gebete.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui de<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_14.lnote.oe.23"/> hloþe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_14.lnote.oe.24"/> fuerit accusatus, abneget per centum uiginti hidas uel sic emendet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="40" ed="#attenborough"/>Se ðe hloþe betygen sie, geswicne<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Ine_14.attnote.fn.9"/> se<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_14.attnote.fn.10"/> hine be CXX hida oððe swa bete<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Ine_14.attnote.fn.11"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="14.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="380" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LVIII} Se ðe hloþe betygen sie, geswicne se hine be CXX hida oððe swa bete.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Wer [der Theilnahme an] einer ‘Bande’ bezichtigt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_14.lnote.de.1"/> ist, der reinige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_14.lnote.de.2"/> sich durch [Eid in Stärke von] 120 Hiden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_14.lnote.de.3"/> oder büsse demgemäss.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_14.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whoever is accused [of taking part in] a ‘band’, let him clear himself by [an oath to the value of] 120 hides or pay accordingly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="41" ed="#attenborough"/>He who is accused of belonging to a band of marauders shall clear himself [of such a charge] with an oath of 120 hides<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_14.attnote.n.1"/>, or pay corresponding compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>He who is accused of [complicity with] a band [of marauders] is to clear himself by [an oath of] 120 hides, or compensate correspondingly.<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_14.whinote.n.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="381" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>He who is accused of taking part in a raid by a band [of thieves], let him clear himself by [an oath of] 120 hides or pay equivalent compensation.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:App-AGu_2-3">App AGu 2.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="381"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11">Af 11</ref> <quote>Swearing oaths in hides occurs only in Ine, Alfred §11</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="90"><ref target="clause:Wi_23-a">Wi 23</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="309"><ref target="clause:Af_11-4">Af 11.4</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hloþ <hi rend="italic">Hk App. A Gu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hloþ Hk App. A Gu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hloþ betogen sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hloþ betogen sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hundtwelftigum hyda <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hundtwelftigum hyda Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gebete <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gebete Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D. h. nicht handhaft ertappt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">I.e. not caught in the act</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Wort zitiert Toller nur aus Ine und vergleicht Gotisch und Nordisch. H setzt einmal, B dreimal modernere Synonyma dafür</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Toller cites the word only from Ine and compares Gothic and Norse. H once, and B three times, substitute more modern synonyms for it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eideshufen 5—9; Eidesschwere 2A</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eideshufen 5—9; Eidesschwere 2A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_14.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nämlich 120 Schill. Strafe ‘Ungehorsam’ (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 11) an den König; <hi rend="italic">s. u.</hi> 15. Dies fordert Af nur, wo ein 1200 Schill.-Mann erschlagen war. — Die Busse an Kläger bleibt unerwähnt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Namely a fine of 120 shill. for ‘disobedience’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 11) to the king; <hi rend="italic">see below</hi> 15. Af demands this only where a 1200-shill. man had been slain. — The compensation to the plaintiff is not mentioned</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_14.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>geswicne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">geclensie</hi>. B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 9 is printed 2 times on the page (14, 15), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_14.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>se</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">he</hi>. Bu.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 10 is printed 2 times on the page (14, 16), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_14.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>bete</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gebete</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_14.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The expression of the value of the oath in hides is found only in the laws of Ine (cf. cap. 19. 46. 52. 53. 54), together with Alf. cap. 11, and the <hi rend="italic">Dialogue of Archbishop Egbert</hi>: <hi rend="italic">Presbiter secundum numerum cxx tributariorum; diaconus vero juxta numerum lx manentium; monachus vero secundum numerum xxx tributariorum, sed hoc in criminali causa.</hi> (Cf. Seebohm, <hi rend="italic">Tribal Custom in A.S. Law</hi>, p. 379 f.) Elsewhere, the value of the oath is expressed in money. The expression of the oath in hides has never been satisfactorily explained, but it may be observed that the number of hides required seems to correspond to the number of shillings involved in the compensation or fine (see Ine, cap. 52; cap. 46. 7. 43; cap. 54. 23; and, for a discussion of this subject, Chadwick, <hi rend="italic">Anglo-Saxon Institutions</hi>, p. 134 ff.). See Liebermann, <hi rend="italic">Die Eideshufen bei den Angelsachsen</hi>, in the <hi rend="italic">Festschrift für Zeumer</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_14.whinote.n.4" n="4" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">401</biblScope></bibl><label>correspondingly</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">When an oath is expressed in hides, their number often corresponds to the number of shillings in the fine, so a fine of 120 shillings is meant.</seg></note>
      </div>
